# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A variable the core defines reads as the language's own"

# A variable an author writes may come from TiddlyWiki's core or from their own `\define`, and the
# name alone carries no mark. So the grammar matches a list, and the list lives in the edition —
# `$:/tw5-syntax/BuiltInVariables` — where an operator weighs an addition against what the core
# documents. `tools/builtins-sync.js` projects it into the grammar, and a gate holds the two
# together, so neither one quietly becomes the source.
#
# Seven exact names come from the tiddlers TiddlyWiki's own documentation tags Core Variables. The
# `tv-` prefix carries the transclusion family, which the core adds to between releases.
#
# Measured over the 65 bundled themes, a core variable reads apart from an author's in 41.

# A core name carries BOTH families: the capture names every macro call, and the core branch
# names this one inside it, so the core family stands innermost and wins.

! A core variable, and an author's beside it

<<currentTiddler>>
# ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ variable.language.builtin.tiddlywiki5

<<myOwnMacro>>
# ^^^^^^^^^^ variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#  ^^^^^^^^^ - variable.language.builtin.tiddlywiki5

! The transclusion family, carried by its prefix

<<tv-story-list>>
# ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ variable.language.builtin.tiddlywiki5

! A name that merely opens with a core name stays the author's

<<currentTiddlerOfMine>>
# ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ variable.name.macro.tiddlywiki5
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ - variable.language.builtin.tiddlywiki5
